**What Bob ate:**
Bob ate **aged organic milk** (which is essentially **curdled/spoiled milk**) tossed over **seasoned tomato purée** spread on **baked whole wheat**.

**Was it healthy?**
**No.** While the ingredients he listed (whole wheat, tomato purée, organic milk) sound healthy on paper, the key word is **"aged."** Aged milk has curdled and spoiled, making it unsafe to eat. Consuming spoiled dairy can cause food poisoning, stomach upset, and other illnesses.

**What happened:**
Alice reacted with **"wtf"** because she realized Bob was eating **spoiled/curdled milk** and thought it was healthy. The photo likely showed lumpy, separated, or discolored dairy that looked unappetizing or clearly rotten, prompting her disgusted reaction. Bob misunderstood "aged" as a positive quality (like aged cheese or wine) rather than recognizing it as spoiled milk. [end of text]


